          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "language": "py",
          "contents": "# CIW AI Associate Standard: 2.2\n# Standard Description: Describe data gathering to create new datasets.\n#\n# Rationale: AI starts with data. But where does it come from? Sometimes we \n# gather it from sensors, surveys, or logs. In this tutorial, we will \"gather\" \n# simulated data using numpy to create a brand new dataset from scratch. \n# This helps students understand the structure of a CSV or Excel file.\n\n\"\"\"\nWelcome! Before an AI can learn, an engineer has to gather the data. \nData \"gathering\" is the process of collecting information and putting it \ninto a structured format (like a table).\n\nToday, we will be \"Digital Scientists\". We are going to gather data about \na fictional forest: the height of trees and their age.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n# --- PART 1: GATHERING RAW OBSERVATIONS ---\nprint(\"--- Part 1: Gathering Observations ---\")\n\n# Imagine we went into the forest and measured 100 trees.\n# We'll use numpy to simulate these measurements.\nnp.random.seed(42) # This makes sure our \"random\" numbers are the same every time\ntree_ages = np.random.randint(1, 50, size=100) # Ages between 1 and 50 years\n# Tree height is usually age * some factor + some noise\ntree_heights = (tree_ages * 2.5) + np.random.normal(0, 5, size=100) \n\nprint(f\"Gathered {len(tree_ages)} observations of Age and Height.\")\n\n# --- PART 2: STRUCTURING THE DATA ---\nprint(\"\\n--- Part 2: Putting Data into a Table (DataFrame) ---\")\n\n# We use pandas to turn these raw lists into a structured \"DataFrame\".\n# Think of a DataFrame as a single sheet in an Excel file.\ndata = {\n    'Tree_ID': range(1, 101),\n    'Age_Years': tree_ages,\n    'Height_Feet': tree_heights\n}\ndf = pd.DataFrame(data)\n\n# Let's look at the first 5 rows we \"gathered\"\nprint(df.head())\n\n# --- PART 3: VISUALIZING THE GATHERED DATA ---\nplt.scatter(df['Age_Years'], df['Height_Feet'], color='green', alpha=0.6)\nplt.title(\"Gathered Forest Data\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Age (Years)\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Height (Feet)\")\nplt.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\nplt.show()\n\n\"\"\"\n--- YOUR TURN ---\nNow it's your turn to gather some data! \nImagine you are gathering data on a \"Coffee Shop\". \n\n1. Create a list called 'customers' with 10 random numbers (1 to 50).\n2. Create a list called 'revenue' which is the number of customers * 5.\n3. Put them into a pandas DataFrame called 'shop_df'.\n\"\"\"\n\n# STARTING CODE FOR STUDENT:\n# TODO: Create the raw data\n# customers = ...\n# revenue = ...\n\n# TODO: Create the DataFrame\n# shop_df = ...\n\n# TODO: Print the DataFrame!\n",
          "folderId": "0",
